      "writtenOn": "2018-12-05T05:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For now, I don\u0027t know how many HID devices will be connected to EC. Do you know ? but still I believe this is the right approach for API.\n\nWhen I design API, first, I should think about how to make it easy for users(clients) to use. That\u0027s my first priority. So I usually create code(client application) first while pretending all API functions are already ready to use. and then see if they are easy and simple. if not, modify here and there to make more simple and easy to use. Try to use common and well-known mechanism. here \"easy\" also includes how to hide any underlying details so that make users to focus on their area. They don\u0027t need to learn. Honestly, I don\u0027t think I introduced any cognitive overhead cost here.",
      "parentUuid": "302154a5_8f5bcd65",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "073ed8313339b43637d8f9b97f9db2d2c4edca8e",
