      "writtenOn": "2018-12-06T06:18:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Caveh,\n\n\u003e\u003e i don\u0027t like is the ## operator for constructing symbols because it makes them hard to find in the src for people who aren\u0027t intimately familiar with what\u0027s going on.\n\nI understand what you mean since I doesn\u0027t like it. but my one(##hid_dev) is simple and what you see in the macro is everything. It\u0027s not complicated like DECLARE_XXX in ECOS.\n\nHonestly I wanted to survive with \"static\" like below but I got multi definition error due to how DECLARE_HOOK() works. so I added \"##hid_dev\".\n\n#define HID_DEVICE_ENTRY(hid_dev) \\\n\tstatic void _hid_dev_entry(void) \\\n\t{ \\\n\t\thid_subsys_register_device(\u0026(hid_dev)); \\\n\t} \\\n\tDECLARE_HOOK(HOOK_INIT, _hid_dev_entry, HOOK_PRIO_LAST - 2)\n\n#endif /* __HID_DEVICE_H */",
      "parentUuid": "b1d64043_5e1ad855",
      "range": {
