      "writtenOn": "2018-12-06T17:47:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the array idea. For EC code, it is common for each individual board to define a array structure for all of the drivers it wants to use.\n\nIf each hid device publicly defined it standard structures/driver, then each board file (e.g. atlas_ish or arcada_ish) would create an array with only the drivers is wanted and potentially any other board level configuration/tuning required.\n\nBelow are a few examples for other drivers. Applying it here: this code would declare an external hid_config_t array structure that would be initialized in every board file that used this driver. Then the ipc_init (or correct function) would just iterate over this array at the correct time.\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/93eee0a9e77bb8bb9726998eb84940ada6010d14/include/usbc_ppc.h#126\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/93eee0a9e77bb8bb9726998eb84940ada6010d14/board/nocturne/board.c#285\n\n\nWhat are your thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "26f51ab0_dd93d318",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 27
      },
