    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c1423d5_26a89bca",
        "filename": "chip/ish/hid_subsys.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-06T00:53:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003e Most \"handle\" identifiers in this EC codebase are 0-based\nFor me, 0 is NULL, invalid handle, and not-suitable for indicating some valid thing(object, whatever) since many well-known APIs don\u0027t use 0 for valid handle. I don\u0027t like returning 0 for valid handle.\n\nI see most ECOS API has different error handling from Linux or other OS.\n\nAnyway, I don\u0027t care. I\u0027ll change it.",
      "parentUuid": "8622a43e_0f16eb70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "073ed8313339b43637d8f9b97f9db2d2c4edca8e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9f865f3_99f454d7",
        "filename": "chip/ish/hid_subsys.c",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-06T17:47:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that a handle of value 0 is a little weird when it is an opaque identifier.\n\nI was getting at that we don\u0027t need any extra layer of handle vs index. I don\u0027t see what it buys us here and it is adding complexity (or at least increases the likelihood of an off-by-1 error) since both handle and index are of the same type.\n\nI think opaque handles are a good idea in some situations, but I don\u0027t think the extra layer is justified here.",
      "parentUuid": "4c1423d5_26a89bca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "073ed8313339b43637d8f9b97f9db2d2c4edca8e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
